        }
      ],
      "id": "kimktnw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xrp9icd",
      "content": "The circulatory system transports oxygen, nutrients, hormones and removes waste products. It consists of Blood, Heart and Blood Vessels."
    },
    {
      "id": "42tkl3l",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "hljrgzz",
      "src": "/books/Precis/RRB GS/images/image_hljrgzz.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "id": "eoafn8h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2 Composition of Blood"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qtn2xo9",
      "content": "Blood is a fluid connective tissue. Normal blood pH is 7.4. Average blood volume in adults is 5–6 litres (about 7% of body weight)."
    },
    {
      "id": "1kujvcc",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Component</p>",
            "<p>Percentage</p>",
            "<p>Main Function</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Plasma</p>",
            "<p>55–60%</p>",
            "<p>Transport medium</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>RBC</p>",
            "<p>40–45%</p>",
            "<p>Oxygen transport</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>WBC</p>",
            "<p>&lt;1%</p>",
            "<p>Immunity</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Platelets</p>",
            "<p>&lt;1%</p>",
            "<p>Clotting</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "j6947ll",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3 Red Blood Cells (RBC)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m23zlkg",
      "content": "• Formed in Bone marrow."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x287e0z",
      "content": "• Life span: 120 days."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p9q4xbw",
      "content": "• No nucleus in mature RBC."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hs7u96c",
      "content": "• Contain Haemoglobin (iron protein)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "608ogso",
      "content": "• Destroyed in Spleen (Graveyard of RBC)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fu7zc5n",
      "content": "• Deficiency causes Anaemia."
    },
    {
      "id": "46qbzg0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4 White Blood Cells (WBC)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "23cwtxt",
      "content": "• Have nucleus."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6dzxfyj",
      "content": "• Fight infection."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jyjjg80",
      "content": "• Formed in bone marrow &amp; lymph nodes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j4i8n38",
      "content": "• Increase: Leukemia."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4a7ato4",
      "content": "<a></a>• Decrease: Leukopenia."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "CHAPTER 4: BLOOD & CIRCULATORY SYSTEM",
      "id": "m7q7031"
    },
